---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Patreon Creators
description: The 3D designers Carey Harwoods, LLC supports on Patreon, Cults3D, and MyMiniFactory — whose models we're licensed to print and sell.
---
<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Our Patreon Creators</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">
      The talented 3D designers we support — and whose models we're licensed to print and sell.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container section-pad">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Every 3D-printed piece we sell starts with a design, and behind every design is an
      artist. We subscribe to these creators through Patreon and their Cults3D or
      MyMiniFactory pages, which gives us a <strong>commercial license</strong> to print
      and sell their work — so the designers get paid for every model we offer.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="creator-grid">
    {% for creator in patreons %}
    <div class="creator-card">
      <span class="creator-platform">{{ creator.platform }}</span>
      <h3>{{ creator.name }}</h3>
      <p>{{ creator.blurb }}</p>
      {% if creator.url %}
      <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;"><a class="creator-link" href="{{ creator.url }}" rel="noopener">Visit their page &rarr;</a></p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        Found something online you'd love to have printed? Let us know! We don't mind
        reaching out to a creator to see if we can get a license to print it for you.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      Message us on <a href="{{ site.social.facebook }}" rel="noopener">Facebook</a>,
      <a href="{{ site.social.instagram }}" rel="noopener">Instagram</a>, or
      <a href="{{ site.social.tiktok }}" rel="noopener">TikTok</a> with a link to the
      model, and we'll take it from there.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
